<title>NORWAY: Norway issues new T-bill SS45 of 5.5 bln crowns.</title>
<headline>Norway issues new T-bill SS45 of 5.5 bln crowns.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's central bank said on Thursday the Finance Ministry issued a new 12-month treasury bill of 5.5 billion crowns, of which 500 million crowns were reserved for the bank.</p>
<p>The T-bill, named SS45, has a coupon of 4.30 percent. Bids should be made by 0900 GMT on December 16. Settlement is two days later. The bill matures on December 17, 1997, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
